---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import StudyNav from "../../components/studies/StudyNav.astro";
import StudyBanner from "../../components/studies/StudyBanner.astro";
import Chip from "../../components/studies/Chip.astro";
import { finance as D, usd, usdM, pct } from "../../data/studies";
const A = D.results.A;
const B = D.results.B;
const fmt = (unit: string, v: number | null) =>
  v === null || v === undefined ? "—" : unit === "%" ? pct(v, 1) : unit.startsWith("USD") ? usd(v) : unit === "x" ? v + "×" : String(v);
const chipKind = (s: string) => (s.startsWith("SOURCED") ? "sourced" : s === "STUDY" ? "study" : "illustrative");
const rows: [string, string, (r: typeof A) => string][] = [
  ["Total development cost", "incl. contingency and capitalized interest", (r) => usdM(r.tdc)],
  ["TDC per bed", "", (r) => usd(r.tdcPerBed)],
  ["TDC per gross sf", "", (r) => usd(r.tdcPerGsf)],
  ["Rent per bed per lease used", "A: UVM anchor · B: required rent", (r) => usd(r.rent)],
  ["  per month of lease", "", (r) => usd(r.rentMonthly)],
  ["Net operating income", "", (r) => usdM(r.noi)],
  ["Annual debt service", "", (r) => usdM(r.debtService)],
  ["Debt-service coverage", "", (r) => (r.dscr ? r.dscr.toFixed(2) + "×" : "n/a")],
  ["Yield on cost", "", (r) => pct(r.yoc, 2)],
  ["Rent per bed per lease for coverage target", "", (r) => usd(r.rentForDscr)],
  ["Rent per bed per lease for yield target", "", (r) => usd(r.rentForYield)],
];
---

<Base
  title="Trinity Rise development model — Ivan Minier"
  theme="studies"
  description="A preliminary, editable development model for a 300-bed Trinity Rise comparing a university public-benefit scenario with a hypothetical premium private scenario. Illustrative inputs are labelled."
>
  <header class="st-hero wrap-wide">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Study B · Development finance</p>
      <h1>A first development model for Trinity Rise</h1>
      <p class="lede">What would a 300-bed apartment building have to charge to pay for itself — and what does "premium" add?</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/studies/trinity-rise-development-model.xlsx" download>Download the workbook (.xlsx) ↓</a>
    </div>
    <StudyBanner>
      This model is separate from the proposal's capital study ($375M–$530M district range; the
      Rise allowance is $90M–$140M) and does not revise it. Many inputs are illustrative
      placeholders with no market basis, and are labelled that way.
    </StudyBanner>
  </header>
  <StudyNav />

  <section class="wrap-wide st-section">
    <span class="st-num">Two scenarios</span>
    <h2>One building, two ways to deliver it.</h2>
    <div class="st-cols">
      <div class="st-card"><h3>A · University, public benefit</h3><p>{D.scenarios.A}</p></div>
      <div class="st-card"><h3>B · Hypothetical premium private <Chip k="scenario" /></h3><p>{D.scenarios.B}</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap-wide st-section">
    <span class="st-num">Results</span>
    <h2>Debt service alone exceeds today's UVM room rate.</h2>
    <div class="st-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Model results">
      <table class="st-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Line</th><th scope="col" class="num">A · University</th><th scope="col" class="num">B · Premium private</th><th scope="col">Note</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {rows.map(([l, n, f]) => <tr><th scope="row">{l}</th><td class="num">{f(A)}</td><td class="num">{f(B)}</td><td>{n}</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
        <caption>300 beds of four-bedroom apartments. Every figure recalculates in the workbook; 85 formula results were checked against an independent Python calculation after LibreOffice recalculation (0 mismatches).</caption>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="st-cols">
      <div class="st-prose">
        <h3>What it means</h3>
        <p>
          At a benchmark cost of about {usd(A.tdcPerBed)} per bed and full debt financing at an
          illustrative 5%, debt service is about {usd(A.debtService / 300)} per bed per year — more than
          UVM's 2026-27 University Heights suite-single rate ($12,090 for a nine-month, room-only
          academic year). Even with zero operating costs, coverage would be only
          {(A.egi / A.debtService).toFixed(2)}×; with operating costs it is {A.dscr!.toFixed(2)}×. Covering 1.20× on the
          building's own rents would take about {usd(A.rentForDscr)} per bed per academic year.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is a <em>project-level</em> test. Universities usually finance housing through
          system-wide revenue bonds, reserves, and gifts, with rates set across all halls, so a
          single building's coverage is not how UVM would judge it. The $12,090 anchor is also a
          different product (a room, not an apartment with a kitchen). A system-level version of
          Scenario A needs UVM data this study does not have.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is not a verdict on Trinity. It says a public-benefit Rise at UVM-like rents would need
          some mix of lower cost, equity or gifts, reserves, a longer-term financing structure, or a
          partner — the same pressure that halted UVM's Catamount Woods apartments in 2024.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="st-prose">
        <h3>Scenario B</h3>
        <p>
          No surveyed market rents were available, so B does not assume one. It reports the rent B
          would need: about {usd(B.rentMonthly)} per bed per month on a 12-month lease to reach an
          illustrative {pct(D.inputs.find((i) => i.key === "yieldTarget")!.B as number, 1)} yield on
          cost. Comparing that with real Burlington-area rents (Redstone Lofts, University Commons,
          Spinner Place, off-campus four-bedrooms) is the next step.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap-wide st-section">
    <span class="st-num">Sensitivity</span>
    <h2>Rent needed for 1.20× coverage, by cost and rate (Scenario A).</h2>
    <div class="st-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Sensitivity of required rent">
      <table class="st-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col" class="num">Cost per bed</th><th scope="col">Benchmark</th>{D.sensitivity.rate.map((r) => <th scope="col" class="num">{pct(r, 0)} rate</th>)}</tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {D.sensitivity.costPerBed.map((c, i) => (
            <tr class={c === 233000 ? "hl" : ""}><td class="num">{usd(c)}</td><td>{D.sensitivity.notes[i]}</td>{D.sensitivity.rent[i].map((v) => <td class="num">{usd(v)}</td>)}</tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
        <caption>Rent per bed per academic year. Compare UVM's $12,090 University Heights suite-single rate (AY 2026-27). Cost benchmarks are from other universities and dates and are not Trinity estimates; the last row is the proposal's own Rise allowance per bed at its upper bound.</caption>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h3>Premium cost vs. extra rent (Scenario B)</h3>
    <div class="st-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Premium sensitivity">
      <table class="st-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col" class="num">Premium cost per bed</th><th scope="col" class="num">Extra rent per bed per month to hold the yield target</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{D.premium.map((p) => <tr><td class="num">{usd(p.premiumPerBed)}</td><td class="num">{usd(p.extraRentPerMonth)}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap-wide st-section">
    <span class="st-num">Inputs</span>
    <h2>Every input, with its basis.</h2>
    <div class="st-legend"><span><Chip k="sourced" /> cited public figure</span><span><Chip k="study" /> from this portfolio's drawings</span><span><Chip k="illustrative" /> placeholder, replace before use</span></div>
    <div class="st-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Model inputs">
      <table class="st-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Input</th><th scope="col" class="num">A</th><th scope="col" class="num">B</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Basis</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {D.inputs.map((i) => (
            <tr><td>{i.label}</td><td class="num">{fmt(i.unit, i.A as number)}</td><td class="num">{fmt(i.unit, i.B as number | null)}</td><td><Chip k={chipKind(i.status)} label={i.status.toLowerCase()} /></td><td>{i.source}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h3>Illustrative timeline</h3>
    <div class="st-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Development timeline">
      <table class="st-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Phase</th><th scope="col" class="num">Months</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{D.timeline.map((t) => <tr><td>{t.phase}</td><td class="num">{t.months}</td></tr>)}<tr class="hl"><th scope="row">Sequential upper bound (phases may overlap)</th><td class="num">{D.timeline.reduce((s, t) => s + t.months, 0)}</td></tr></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
